620\"><img src=\"https://link.axios.com/img/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94asujod.747j/6df655b0.gif\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding-right:3.5%\" align=\"right\"> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lLTk2ZmVmZDI2LWNiNTEtNGQ5ZS04YWZiLWJiYWY1ZGJmZmViMS5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBcb6a2dad\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"b\" style=\"color:#222;font-size:13px;font-family:'gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-decoration:underline\">View in browser</a> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"30\" style=\"height:30px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>  <tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.3\"> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"16\" style=\"height:16px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1\">\r\n<span class=\"s\" style=\"font-size:44px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#008dc8;letter-spacing:-1px;line-height:1\"> Axios Finish Line </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.5;padding-bottom:35px;padding-top:10px\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">By  Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei  <span style=\"margin:0 6px\">&middot;</span> Nov 16, 2026 </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.75;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;padding:0 3.5%\"><p><strong>Hello, Monday! </strong><em>Smart Brevity™ count: 429 words … 1½ mins. Edited by Natalie Daher and copy edited by Amy Stern.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: 30-second stress reset </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/sutvzdcP3r83FrGZwbSXxLXanm8=/0x0:1280x720/2026/11/16/1794864648288.gif\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Animated illustration of a red, shaking stopwatch. The button clicks, and the second hand moves 30 seconds, while the stopwatch stops shaking and the red color fades to reveal a silver and white stopwatch.\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>I've tried <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly9lbi53aWtpcGVkaWEub3JnL3dpa2kvUG93ZXJfcG9zaW5nP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBd654e26d\" target=\"_blank\">power posing</a>,</strong> I've done <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly9kaHdibG9nLmR1a2VoZWFsdGgub3JnL21hc3RlcmluZy1ib3gtYnJlYXRoaW5nLWEtc2ltcGxlLXRlY2huaXF1ZS10by1yZWxpZXZlLXN0cmVzcy8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB68158a0f\" target=\"_blank\">box breathing</a>, I've taken supplements. Nothing quite shakes off the scaries like somatic movement — and if my Instagram <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaW5zdGFncmFtLmNvbS9yZWVsL0RkZkd5WTNnbWF4JTIwP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB163a3f23\" target=\"_blank\">algorithm</a> is <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaW5zdGFncmFtLmNvbS9yZWVsL0RiaUprZUtSWV9NLz9ycHh0PU5uVmpjblIyYjJsc2R6aDQmdXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBc03eeca6\" target=\"_blank\">any indication</a>, I'm not alone, <em>Axios' Natalie Daher writes</em>.</p><ul><li><strong>🫨 Why it matters:</strong> Sometimes the best way to calm your mind is to move your body. A simple technique called <em>somatic shaking</em> may help loosen muscle tension, interrupt anxious thoughts and give your brain a reset.</li></ul><p><strong>All you need </strong>is 30 seconds and a little room to move. </p><ul><li><strong>Maybe that's a restroom </strong>or beside your bed in the morning, rather than a subway platform, but you do you. </li></ul><p><strong>Here's how to try it,</strong> per University of Virginia psychologist Kim Penberthy and other experts <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly90aW1lLmNvbS9hcnRpY2xlLzIwMjYvMTEvMTAvc29tYXRpYy1zaGFraW5nLXN0cmVzcy1yZWxpZWYvP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBd2c8b678\" target=\"_blank\">interviewed by TIME</a>: </p><ol><li><strong>👋 Start with your hands. </strong>Shake them gently for 10–15 seconds, as if you're flicking off water.</li><li><strong>🙆 Get your arms involved. </strong>Keep your shoulders loose and let your arms shake naturally. Think inflatable tube man outside a car dealership. OK, maybe not <em>that </em>naturally.</li><li><strong>🦵 Shake out your legs. </strong>Move one at a time, holding onto something for balance if needed.</li><li><strong>😮‍💨 Pause and notice. </strong>Do your shoulders feel less tense? Has your mind quieted down? Where might you still be holding tension?</li></ol><p><strong>The big picture:</strong> You can't always think your way out of stress, especially when you're overstimulated. Sometimes a little physical movement can help break the cycle.</p><ul><li><strong>The best part? </strong>You can do it between meetings, after a difficult phone call or whenever you need a quick reset.</li></ul><p><strong>💃 The bottom line: </strong>Shaking off what ails us is a small reminder not to take ourselves too seriously — and that even our most anxious moments, too, shall pass.</p><p><strong><em>P.S.</em> Tonight is my last Finish Line! </strong>A heartfelt thank-you to Mike, Erica, Amy, our dedicated readers and Axios for letting me share these stories with you over the years.</p><ul><li><strong>A few parting words: </strong>Marathon-running was a <em>wild </em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjQvMDUvMDgvbWFyYXRob24tcnVubmluZy10cmFpbmluZy10aWt0b2s_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB2ec86298\" target=\"_blank\">quarter-life crisis</a>, <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lLWQ0MWZkYTYwLWRlOTctMTFlZi04ZGFhLWQ1MzAxYWVhZTc2MC5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB5aefd296\" target=\"_blank\">chores with friends</a> are way more fun, and it's never too early to start <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lLWRhMTAyYWY1LTBlYzAtNGRmMi04ODJjLWM3N2MzNzk4MzE1OS5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB07f8eae6\" target=\"_blank\">documenting your family history</a> (chosen or biological). </li><li><strong>Plus:</strong> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMDkvMDkvaG93LXRvLWZpZ2h0LW1vcmUtYXJ0ZnVsbHktcHJpeWEtcGFya2VyP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBa65e442c\" target=\"_blank\">Handling conflict is a skill</a>, and nothing beats an <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMDUvMTMvc2luZ2xlcy1ldmVudHMtZGF0aW5nLWFwcC1mYXRpZ3VlP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB2c75fc43\" target=\"_blank\">in-person hang</a>.</li></ul><p><strong>Thanks for reading along. ❤️</strong></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtOTZmZWZkMjYtY2I1MS00ZDllLThhZmItYmJhZjVkYmZmZWIxLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB80d25778\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48454429.332047/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_dGV